[C1] PASS a uniform flux on a Cartesian block gives a bitwise zero tendency: max |div| = 0.0e+00 over 5x4x3 cells; the equal face areas make the two terms of each direction cancel exactly, not just to round-off
[C2] PASS the spherical-polar areas and volume give div(r rhat) = 3 to round-off: max |div - 3| = 3.55e-15 over a 6x5x4 block (this is the identity tests/test_cubed_sphere_cell_volume.py asserts per cell)
[C3] PASS the cell volume uses the exact radial integral (r_+^3 - r_-^3)/3, not r^2 dr: exact minus midpoint = h**3/12, so the midpoint form would be short by h^3/12 per unit solid angle
[C4] PASS sum of V times the divergence equals the net flux through the block boundary: relative difference 1.90e-16 on random face fluxes, so the operator is in flux form and conserves by construction
[C5] PASS lmars is consistent: equal left and right states give the exact physical flux: max |flux - exact| = 8.9e-16; pbar = p and ubar = u exactly (the jump terms carry (u_l - u_r) and (p_l - p_r))
[C6] PASS the face velocity carries the pressure jump over rho c, and the face pressure carries the velocity jump times rho c: a pure pressure jump of 0.2 drives ubar = -0.080582; two states converging at 0.3 raise pbar to 1.354965 above the mean 1.0
[C7] PASS the dry row plus every species row is the total mass flux: |sum of mass rows - ubar rho| = 1.1e-16; the dry row carries rd = 1 - sum(y) so the split is exact with 3 species
[C8] PASS ivx = IPR - dim rotates the three momentum rows into the face-local frame: dim 1: normal row 3, tangential 1 and 2; dim 2: normal row 2, tangential 3 and 1; dim 3: normal row 1, tangential 2 and 3 -- a permutation of the momentum rows for every direction
8/8 claims pass
